 "result_text": "Fixed: the order of magic and non-magic patterns no longer changes the `glob` result.\n\nThe cause was what the issue described. In `Glob.glob()` in `wcmatch/glob.py`, a non-magic pattern assigned its starting directory to `curdir`. That overwrote the base directory the next magic pattern then searched from. I switched the non-magic branch to a separate `start_dir` variable, so `curdir` stays at the current directory.\n\nI checked it in the repo directory with `['**/setup.py', 'dummy', '**/glob.py']`. Both that order and its reverse return `['wcmatch/glob.py']`. I didn't run the test suite, and I didn't change or add any tests or commit anything.",
